window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f30701136d88f56c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"write-a-weekly-work-summary\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">撰写每周工作总结</h1> <p>将一周的工作活动整理成可提交给经理的进展更新。</p> <p>将日历、编辑过的文档、已发送的消息、跟踪表和项目背景提供给 ChatGPT，再请它总结已完成的工作、决策、变化、阻碍、后续事项和下一阶段重点，并附上来源链接。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要定期撰写周报的经理和个人贡献者。</li> <li>需要从多个工作工具中还原进展的团队。</li> <li>需要区分已确认事实和推断，并附上来源链接的工作更新。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-calendar（需联网）</a></td> <td>还原这一周中的会议和里程碑。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>查看相关工作频道中的已发消息、决策、阻碍和后续事项。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>阅读跟踪表、项目文档以及记录变化的文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>将来源材料整理成清晰、可编辑的每周更新。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>起草我的每周工作更新</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>low</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">我要撰写 [week or date range] 的每周工作更新。\n\n请使用我的日历、我编辑过的文档、我在 [channels] 中发送的消息、[main tracker or planning doc]，以及其他明显相关的背景资料。撰写一份可以提交给经理的总结，涵盖：\n\n- 已完成的工作\n- 已作出的决策\n- 重要变化\n- 阻碍\n- 后续事项\n- 下周优先事项\n\n尽可能附上来源链接。将已确认的事实与推断分开，不要发送或发布这份更新。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：日常工作（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent 技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"reconstruct-the-week-from-source-activity\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">根据工作来源还原这一周</h2> <p>有用的周报不应依赖你回忆每一次会议或消息。请将跟踪表、文档、日历和工作频道消息提供给 ChatGPT，再让它区分已经完成的工作和计划或假设。</p> <ol> <li>明确周报的时间范围和读者。</li> <li>指定涉及的跟踪表、文档、日历和频道。</li> <li>使用起始提示词，并要求重要说法提供来源链接。</li> <li>根据相关讨论串核对决策、阻碍和后续事项。</li> <li>按周报发布位置调整篇幅和语气，但不要自动发布。</li> </ol> <p>要明确区分推断与已确认工作。这样经理或协作者无需重新阅读所有资料，就能发现并纠正问题。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-next-update\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">为下一次更新做准备</h2> <p>第一份总结准确后，可以请 ChatGPT 在下一个汇报周期复用同样的结构，并说明与上一版相比有哪些变化。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the same structure for the next weekly update.\n\nCompare it with the previous update and identify:\n\n- work newly completed\n- decisions that changed\n- blockers that remain\n- follow-ups that moved owners or dates\n- next priorities that are supported by current source context\n\nKeep source links and separate confirmed facts from inferences. Return a draft only.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">下一次每周更新继续采用相同结构。\n\n与上一次更新对比，并指出：\n\n- 新完成的工作\n- 发生变化的决定\n- 仍然存在的阻碍\n- 负责人或日期发生变化的后续事项\n- 当前来源上下文能够支持的下一步优先事项\n\n保留来源链接，将已确认事实与推断分开。只返回草稿。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"write-a-weekly-work-summary\">Write a weekly work summary</h1> <p>Turn a week of activity into a manager-ready update.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT your calendar, edited documents, sent messages, tracker, and project context, then ask it to summarize completed work, decisions, changes, blockers, follow-ups, and next priorities with source links.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Managers and individual contributors writing a recurring weekly update.</li> <li>Teams that need to reconstruct progress from several work surfaces.</li> <li>Updates that should distinguish confirmed facts from inference and include source links.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-calendar (online)</a></td> <td>Reconstruct the meetings and milestones that shaped the week.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Review sent messages, decisions, blockers, and follow-ups in the relevant work channels.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read the tracker, project docs, and files that show what changed.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Turn the source review into a clear, editable weekly update.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Draft my weekly update</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>low</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">I'm writing my weekly update for [week or date range].\n\nUse my calendar, documents I edited, messages I sent in [channels], [main tracker or planning doc], and any other context that is clearly relevant. Write a manager-ready summary covering:\n\n- work completed\n- decisions made\n- important changes\n- blockers\n- follow-ups\n- next week's priorities\n\nInclude source links where possible. Separate confirmed facts from inferences, and do not send or publish the update.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Everyday work (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"reconstruct-the-week-from-source-activity\">Reconstruct the week from source activity</h2> <p>A useful weekly update should not depend on remembering every meeting or message. Point ChatGPT to the tracker, documents, calendar, and work-channel messages that represent the week, then ask it to separate completed work from plans or assumptions.</p> <ol> <li>Define the week and the audience for the update.</li> <li>Name the tracker, documents, calendar, and channels that are in scope.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and ask for source links behind important claims.</li> <li>Check decisions, blockers, and follow-ups against the underlying threads.</li> <li>Revise the length and tone for the destination without publishing it automatically.</li> </ol> <p>Keep inferences visibly separate from confirmed work. This makes it easier for a manager or collaborator to correct the update without rereading every source.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-next-update\">Prepare the next update</h2> <p>Once the first summary is accurate, ask ChatGPT to reuse its structure for the next reporting period and call out what changed since the prior version.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the same structure for the next weekly update.\n\nCompare it with the previous update and identify:\n\n- work newly completed\n- decisions that changed\n- blockers that remain\n- follow-ups that moved owners or dates\n- next priorities that are supported by current source context\n\nKeep source links and separate confirmed facts from inferences. Return a draft only.\n</code></pre>"};
